Subject: [CHANGE] Put ia64 config files on the arm diet
Message-Id: <4c3ccc2f5787b1fb1@agluck-desktop.sc.intel.com>
List-Id: <linux-ia64.vger.kernel.org>
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset="us-ascii"
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 7bit
To: linux-ia64@vger.kernel.org

arch/arm config files were slimmed down using a python script
(See commit c2330e286f68f1c408b4aa6515ba49d57f05beae comment)

Do the same for ia64 so we can have sleek & trim looking
defconfig files too.

Signed-off-by: Tony Luck <tony.luck@intel.com>

---

Patch is pretty unreadable to human eyes - but a lot of lines from
the ia64 defconfig files can be deleted with no side effects (the
.config file resulting from "make xxx_defconfig" is identical to the
one that was generated before this patch is applied.

Patch is too big to post, and as mentioned unreadable. So I just list
the new versions of each file below.

-Tony

